This is Kodia, an AI code editor forked from VS Code (by way of Void).

Kodia's own code lives in src/vs/workbench/contrib/void (the React UI is in its browser/react folder) and in src/vs/platform/agentHost/node/kodia (the Kodia agent). Everything else is VS Code. KODIA_CODEBASE_GUIDE.md explains how the code fits together.

Changing VS Code files outside those folders makes every upstream merge harder: keep such changes minimal, add a "Kodia:" comment explaining why, and say so before making them.

In TypeScript, don't cast unless it's necessary, and never cast to 'any': find the right type. Follow the surrounding file's style, including its use of semicolons, and keep changes as small as the task allows.

Name a map from A to B "bOfA", e.g. toolNameOfToolId.

Check changes with the commands in HOW_TO_CONTRIBUTE.md ("Before opening a pull request"): ESLint, the React build and typecheck, the workbench typecheck, and npm run test-void. Commit messages follow Conventional Commits.
